# @vbcdx/vbcdx — literal configuration template (`vbcdx --env=` and `vbcdx-dev-agents init --env=`).
#
# This file is READ LITERALLY. It is never sourced, executed, or interpolated:
# a $VAR, a ~, or a `$(...)` stays literal. The operator fills in final values
# here; sourcing a shell beforehand does not expand anything in this file.
#
# Grammar: blank lines and lines whose first non-whitespace character is `#`
# are ignored. An assignment splits at the first `=`; surrounding whitespace is
# trimmed. Unquoted values keep interior spaces, `#`, `=`, and `$` literally.
# Single-quoted values are literal; double-quoted values use JSON escaping.
# All paths are absolute. Duplicate keys (including case-equivalent) are errors.

# `vbcdx` without --env reads no file: it uses the harness's own home variable when
# it is set in the environment (CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, CODEX_HOME, OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR,
# HERMES_HOME), otherwise the harness's documented default under $HOME, and
# keeps its state under $HOME/.vbcdx. Codex skills always go to $HOME/.agents/skills.
# With --env, this file pins every directory and those variables are not read.
# `vbcdx doctor` also reads the variables each installed tool declares in its
# vbcdx.json, to report them as set or not set (never their values).

# ── Required installer directories ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Installer state and the installation manifest root.
VBCDX_AGENTS_BASE_DIR=/home/example/.local/state/vbcdx-agents
# Root under which per-role credential files are written (0700). Need not exist
# when no credential files are needed.
VBCDX_AGENTS_CREDENTIALS_DIR=/home/example/.config/vbcdx/credentials

# ── Selected harness root (only the one you install into is required) ────────
# Required for user scope of the matching harness. Project scope uses the
# containing Git worktree instead. These installer keys are translated to the
# harness's own launch environment variables for user scope
# (VBCDX_AGENTS_CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR -> CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, and so on).
# VBCDX_AGENTS_CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/home/example/.config/claude
# VBCDX_AGENTS_CODEX_HOME=/home/example/.codex
# VBCDX_AGENTS_OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR=/home/example/.config/opencode
# VBCDX_AGENTS_HERMES_HOME=/home/example/.hermes

# ── Overlays (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Absolute overlay directories, separated by `:`, applied after any --overlay.
# VBCDX_AGENTS_OVERLAY_DIRS=/home/example/.config/vbcdx/overlays/acme-dev

# ── Hermes model routing (hermes harness only; nonsecret; optional) ──────────
# Hermes profiles cannot run without a model section. With both set, every
# profile gets a named custom provider whose key is read by Hermes from the
# profile's own .env as HERMES_PROVIDER_API_KEY (never from this file).
# VBCDX_AGENTS_HERMES_BASE_URL=https://llm.example/v1
# VBCDX_AGENTS_HERMES_MODEL=provider/model-name
# Optional per-role override (suffix as for credentials):
# VBCDX_AGENTS_HERMES_MODEL_CODE_AGENT=provider/coder-model

# ── Hermes web search (hermes harness only; nonsecret; optional) ─────────────
# For the roles whose descriptor declares web_search: the profile gets the web-litellm-search plugin,
# pointed at this LiteLLM gateway and search tool. The tool is a
# search_tool_name configured on that gateway (its /v1/search/<name> route).
# Set both or neither; there is no default gateway. Unset, those roles are
# written without web search. The key is the profile's own
# HERMES_PROVIDER_API_KEY, read from its .env (never from this file).
# VBCDX_AGENTS_HERMES_WEB_SEARCH_URL=https://llm.example.com
# VBCDX_AGENTS_HERMES_WEB_SEARCH_TOOL=example-search

# ── Optional context and integrations ───────────────────────────────────────
# Informational only; never applied to any server configuration.
# VBCDX_AGENTS_CODE_HOST_URL=https://git.example.com
# Absolute path to the integrations JSON (see README, "Integrations file").
# Omit it when tools are registered with `vbcdx install tool`.
# VBCDX_AGENTS_INTEGRATIONS_FILE=/home/example/.config/vbcdx/integrations.json

# ── Reserved ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VBCDX_AGENTS_WORKDIR is reserved and unsupported when nonblank; leave it out.

# ── A2A cards server runtime (bin/a2a-server.js) ────────────────────
# Runtime configuration for the standalone A2A cards HTTP server. These are read
# from the process environment by that server only; the installer ignores them.
# All are optional and non-secret — the server publishes public cards and needs
# no credentials. Set PUBLIC_BASE_URL on the deployment so the absolute HTTPS
# card URLs are correct; when unset it is derived per request from the Host
# header. PORT defaults to 8080 and HOST to 0.0.0.0. VBCDX_A2A_PACKS names the
# agent packs to serve (comma-separated npm package names or paths); unset, every
# installed agent pack is served, and with none the server refuses to start.
# PORT=8080
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://agents.example
# VBCDX_A2A_PACKS=@example/agent-pack

# ── Hermes profile .env keys (read by Hermes, not by vbcdx) ─────────────────
# These go in a Hermes profile's own .env. A role given read-only git access
# (`git_roles` in the integrations file) needs a Forgejo token scoped
# `read:repository` and the matching scope declaration:
# VBCDX_FORGEJO_GIT_TOKEN=
# VBCDX_FORGEJO_GIT_TOKEN_SCOPE=read:repository
# A web-search role needs its LiteLLM key, and may override the gateway URL and
# search tool:
# HERMES_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
# LITELLM_SEARCH_BASE=https://llm.example.com
# LITELLM_SEARCH_TOOL=example-search

# ── Optional credentials, one file per role and tool ────────────────────────
# Installing agents without any credentials is fully supported. To have vbcdx
# write <CREDENTIALS_DIR>/<role>/<tool>.env, set that role's fields for the tool.
# The suffix is the role id, two underscores, then the tool name, upper-cased
# with hyphens as underscores (code-agent on forgejo -> CODE_AGENT__FORGEJO).
# A Forgejo file needs USER and TOKEN (or PASSWORD); other tools need TOKEN.
# `vbcdx packs` lists the role ids.
#
# VBCDX_AGENTS_USER_CODE_AGENT__FORGEJO=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_TOKEN_CODE_AGENT__FORGEJO=
# VBCDX_AGENTS_TOKEN_DEVOPS_AGENT__COOLIFY=
